WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.370
Rain, snow, fog, humidity, dust, salt spray,

00:00:03.370 --> 00:00:07.070
and other moisture or particles can affect aircraft, sensors, motors, cooling,

00:00:07.070 --> 00:00:08.420
and electrical systems.

00:00:08.420 --> 00:00:10.965
Water resistance varies by model and configuration;

00:00:10.965 --> 00:00:12.925
it should never be assumed from appearance.

00:00:12.925 --> 00:00:16.890
Precipitation adds weight, changes propeller and surface behavior, obscures lenses,

00:00:16.890 --> 00:00:18.445
and can damage components.

00:00:18.445 --> 00:00:21.005
Snow and fog reduce contrast and depth cues.

00:00:21.005 --> 00:00:24.540
Dust or spray can contaminate moving parts and create long-term corrosion after an

00:00:24.540 --> 00:00:26.045
apparently normal flight.

00:00:26.045 --> 00:00:28.710
Visibility must support awareness of the aircraft, hazards,

00:00:28.710 --> 00:00:31.999
and surrounding airspace under applicable rules and operational needs.

00:00:31.999 --> 00:00:34.160
Haze, fog, blowing snow, rain, dust,

00:00:34.160 --> 00:00:37.605
and low cloud can reduce visibility faster than an operator expects.

00:00:37.605 --> 00:00:41.660
Lens obstruction can make the payload product unusable even when the aircraft remains

00:00:41.660 --> 00:00:42.510
controllable.

00:00:42.510 --> 00:00:44.800
Water droplets, condensation, snow, dust,

00:00:44.800 --> 00:00:47.925
or fogging may create false features and poor measurements.

00:00:47.925 --> 00:00:51.400
Do not continue solely to finish a route when data quality has failed.

00:00:51.400 --> 00:00:52.400
Cancellation is a safety control.

00:00:52.400 --> 00:00:56.010
If the aircraft is not approved for the conditions, visibility is inadequate,

00:00:56.010 --> 00:00:58.359
or moisture is increasing, delay or stop.

00:00:58.359 --> 00:01:02.800
A forecast break in weather is not a substitute for acceptable observed conditions.

00:01:02.800 --> 00:01:06.520
After exposure, power down and inspect equipment according to approved guidance.

00:01:06.520 --> 00:01:09.865
Address moisture, contamination, and corrosion before another flight,

00:01:09.865 --> 00:01:13.100
and record abnormal exposure in maintenance or operational logs.
